meta {
  name: POST /memory/index?file=episodic/...&collections=decisions — md → decisions
  type: http
  seq: 93
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/memory/index?collections=decisions&file={{indexFileKey}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

query {
  collections: decisions
  file: {{indexFileKey}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("indexed exactly one chunk into the decisions collection", function() {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.status).to.equal("indexed");
    expect(body.collections).to.be.an("object");
    expect(body.collections.decisions).to.be.a("number");
    expect(body.collections.decisions).to.be.at.least(1);
  });
}

docs {
  The EOD-memo → decisions flow proven live 2026-05-15 with v1.0.22
  + the Keycloak scope grant (PR #87 / #88). A markdown file is
  uploaded to MinIO under ``episodic/`` (typical operator use:
  end-of-day ADR or memo) then re-indexed into the ``decisions``
  ChromaDB collection for semantic recall.

  Last night's 403 on this same flow was the motivating bug for
  the v1.0.22 scope-grant cycle — the audittrace-opencode JWT lacked
  the right scope to call /memory/index. Today: 200, evidence at
  ~/work/audittrace-evidence/20260515-v1.0.22-e2e/.

  Pre-req: the file must already be in MinIO. Use the sibling bru
  ``seed-file.bru`` or ``upload-pdf.bru`` (despite the name it accepts
  .md too) to land the file.

  ``indexFileKey`` (added ADR-062 Phase B / #426, 2026-08-05) is the
  FULL ``?file=`` key exactly as returned by ``POST /memory/upload``'s
  ``key`` response field — since WU-B5, ``/memory/upload`` writes to
  the caller's PRIVATE tier and returns
  ``"{jwt.sub}/{layer}/{filename}"``, not the legacy
  ``"{layer}/{filename}"`` shape. Passing the private-tier key through
  unchanged is exactly the deploy-helper round-trip contract
  (``scripts/deploy/memory.py::log_deploy_record``) and the fleet
  self-log → decisions fold path #426 restores. The env default
  (``episodic/{{exampleAdrFile}}``-shaped) preserves the legacy
  corpus/shared-tier demo for callers who seeded a file directly under
  ``episodic/`` in the shared bucket rather than via ``/memory/upload``.

  Authorization: ``memory:episodic:write`` (or ``memory:procedural:write``
  for a procedural key) — gated on the RESOLVED layer, matching
  ``indexFileKey``'s layer segment, not the target collection.
  ``memory:decisions:write`` is in the issued token (cluster.bru env,
  v1.0.22+) but not runtime-required for this call today — see the doc
  on ``index-single-file.bru`` for the forward-looking enforcement
  story.
}
